      "message": "In August when Go 1.25.0 is released, the go directive in go.mod will be bumped to `go 1.24.0`, so checking for the pre-release version will stop being needed.\n\nIt\u0027s fine as is, but you could also write it in a way that minimizes the upcoming diff to be easier to delete.\n\nSomething like this that leads to a trivial future diff:\n\n```diff\n-if runtime.Version() \u003d\u003d \"go1.24rc1\" {\n-    // Rare path. (This entire block will be deleted in a few months.)\n-    [...]\n-}\n-\n // Common path. (This block will stay behind.)\n [...]\n```",
